nical evaluation and validation of Genos’s architecture, training convergence, and performance across standard benchmarks. Conclusions This work provides a reliable technical blueprint and performance benchmark for the development of the next generation of high-efficiency genomic foundation models. Genos model weights, inference code, and usage documentation are publicly available on GitHub (https://github.com/BGI-HangzhouAI/Genos) and Hugging Face Hub (https://huggingface.co/BGI-HangzhouAI).",exclude_uncertain_unstable,UNCERTAIN,EC3_not_generative,text_component_unclear,primary_model_paper,unclear,unclear,no,yes,omics-text cross-modal diagnostic capabilities,omics-text cross-modal diagnostic capabilities,none,clear_exclude,"Genos is a genomic foundation model for sequence modeling; no explicit generative mechanism described (e.g., decoder, autoregressive, diffusion). Text component and text-bio bridge are unclear from abstract; only ambiguous 'omics-text cross-modal' phrase. Therefore excluded as not generative (EC3).",The abstract describes a genomic foundation model for sequence modeling with no clear natural-language text component; only a vague mention of 'omics-text cross-modal diagnostic capabilities' without detail.,"The abstract describes a genomic foundation model (Genos) for sequence modeling and simulation of noncoding variant effects on expression, but no generative mechanism (e.g., autoregressive, decoder, text generation) is mentioned.","Genos is a genomic foundation model for sequence modeling; no explicit generative mechanism described (e.g., decoder, autoregressive, diffusion). Text component and text-bio bridge are unclear from abstract; only ambiguous 'omics-text cross-modal' phrase. Therefore excluded as not generative (EC3).",Genos: a human-centric genomic foundation model.,"Abstract Background The rapid expansion of human genomic data demands foundation models that manage ultra-long sequences and capture population diversity, limitations commo