and performance across standard benchmarks. Conclusions This work provides a reliable technical blueprint and performance benchmark for the development of the next generation of high-efficiency genomic foundation models. Genos model weights, inference code, and usage documentation are publicly available on GitHub (https://github.com/BGI-HangzhouAI/Genos) and Hugging Face Hub (https://huggingface.co/BGI-HangzhouAI).",exclude_uncertain_unstable,UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,primary_model_paper,unclear,unclear,no,yes,omics-text cross-modal diagnostic capabilities,omics-text cross-modal diagnostic capabilities,none,thin_abstract_boundary,"The abstract clearly presents a new genomic foundation model (primary_model_paper) and includes a biological modality (genomic sequences). It mentions ""omics-text cross-modal diagnostic capabilities,"" but does not explicitly describe natural-language text inputs or outputs, leaving the presence of a text component and a text‑bio bridge ambiguous. No generative mechanism (decoder, autoregressive, diffusion, etc.) is reported, so the model is non‑generative.","The paper introduces a new genomic foundation model (Genos) and clearly involves a biological modality (human genomic sequences). The abstract mentions ""omics-text cross-modal diagnostic capabilities,"" suggesting a text component, but it does not specify natural-language text or a concrete text‑bio mapping, leaving the presence of a substantive text component and bridge ambiguous.","The abstract presents Genos as a genomic foundation model with large‑scale pretraining but does not describe a decoder, autoregressive or other generative mechanism, so no generative model is evident; foundation‑model characteristics are clearly stated.","The abstract clearly presents a new genomic foundation model (primary_model_paper) and includes a biological modality (genomic sequences). It mentions ""omics-text cross-modal diagnostic capabilities,"" but does not explicitly describe natural-