/Users/bogdan.didenko/lpnu/review/docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:13577:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nFigure type: conceptual biological hierarchy diagram.\n\nVisible labels: “Genome Book” at the top, branching to “Chromosome 1,” “Chromosome 2,” and “……”. Under Chromosome 1, nested labels include “ChromosomePart1,” “ChromosomePart2,” “DNA Chapter1,” “DNA Chapter2,” “DNA Section1,” “DNASection2,” “DNA para 1,” and “DNA para 2.”\n\nAxes/panels/legend: no axes, panels, scale bars, or legend are visible.\n\nBiological/model quantity shown: an analogy or hierarchical organization of genomic DNA, representing the genome as a book and chromosomes/DNA subdivisions as nested textual units.\n\nMain visible finding: the image illustrates that a genome can be organized hierarchically from chromosomes down to smaller DNA sections/paragraph-like units.",
