/Users/bogdan.didenko/lpnu/review/data/docling_graph_screening_evidence_full_2026-07-10_gpt54mini_direct_nolimits_16shards/shard_07/full_2026-07-06__rec_002243/screening_evidence_summary.json:2983:            "Human Genome Book: Words, Sentences and Paragraphs",
/Users/bogdan.didenko/lpnu/review/data/docling_graph_screening_evidence_full_2026-07-10_gpt54mini_direct_nolimits_16shards/shard_07/full_2026-07-06__rec_002243/screening_evidence_summary.json:2992:          "text": "For  model  selection,  we  again  adopted  the  GPT2LMHeadModel,  which  is  based  on  GPT-2  and specically  designed  for  causal  language  modeling  tasks.  Since  GPT-2  does  not  directly  support Seq2Seq problems, we indirectly achieved this by formatting the training samples. Specically, each training sample was organized into the format '[Original Text] TL;DR: [Summary]', where 'TL;DR:' serves as a prompt to guide the model in understanding the relationship between the input text and the  target  summary.  During  training,  the  model  learned  to  generate  concise  summaries  from  long texts  by  maximizing  the  log-likelihood  estimation  of  the  training  data,  while  preserving  the  core information of the input text.",
